<WRAP center round important 70%>
**Warning!** Don't brick your router!

There is 1% probability that devices with the ''Foresee'' NAND flash chip can be shipped from factory with remapped **Bad Blocks**. Please use special [[https://github.com/dimfishr/openwrt/releases/tag/filogic-2025-02-17|Test Build PR #17963]]. For more information see [[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/17963|PR #17963]]
 
</WRAP>

<WRAP center round important 70%>
**Warning!** Don't brick your router!

There is 1% probability that devices with the ''Winbond'' NAND flash (which have bad blocks) will brick during OpenWrt installation. OpenWrt 23.05-SNAPSHOT and 24.10.0 releases are affected. The fix is already present in SNAPSHOT and 24.10-SNAPSHOT builds and will be present in 24.10.1 release.
 
</WRAP>

<WRAP center round important 70%>
**Warning!** Don't brick your router!

To ensure compatibility with all existing AX3000T hardware types for RD03 and RD23, OpenWrt version [[:releases:24.10:notes-24.10.0|24.10.0]] is recommended.

→ **Don’t try to flash other versions without checking your router hardware!**: [[:inbox:toh:xiaomi:ax3000t#hardware_support_status|details]].

</WRAP>

The Xiaomi AX3000T router is based on the MediaTek Filogic 820 SoC (MediaTek MT7981B) in the RD03 and RD23 models, and the Qualcomm IPQ5018 SoC in the RD03v2 model. It supports two 802.11ax streams on both 2.4GHz @40MHz and 5GHz @160MHz for a combined 3000Mbps wireless speed. 

There are three versions of the Xiaomi AX3000T router:
  * model **RD03**: Chinese version
  * model **RD23**: International (Global) version.
  * model **RD03v2**: New Chinese version with Qualcomm SoC. <color red>**Not supported.**</color>
Both RD03 and RD23 versions have exactly the same hardware, and the only difference is the version of the stock firmware (which is region-locked).

{{:media:xiaomi:xiaomi_ax3000t.jpg?480|AX3000T}}

**Support Forums** https://forum.openwrt.org/t/openwrt-support-for-xiaomi-ax3000t/180490

There are 2 known OpenWrt installation methods for the Xiaomi AX3000T:
  * **API RCE method**: the method involves executing shell commands on the stock router firmware to enable SSH access by exploiting the API RCE, either in ''xqsystem/start_binding'' or ''misystem/arn_switch'', depending on the firmware version. This method is suitable for both **RD23** (International version) and **RD03** (Chinese version) of the Xiaomi AX3000T router. For details, please refer to the [[:inbox:toh:xiaomi:ax3000t#installation|Installation]] section below. 
  * **UART flash method**: the method which requires opening the device, connecting a UART cable, and following a specific set of steps. This process is recommended only for advanced users and may soft brick your device. The instructions for this process are available in this post: [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/openwrt-support-for-xiaomi-ax3000t/180490/420?u=alexq|link to owrt forum]].

